PHP-FIG (Framework Interoperability Group): defines standards to ensure interops between PHP components

[in composer.json]
-> psr-4 : PHP STATNDARD RECOMMANDATION
standard for autoloading classes form file paths.
=> before php 5: use `require` in each file I need the module
-- gestion des dependances fastidieuse
=> Then php 5: spl_autoload_register(function($class){...})
-- auto includes the module file when the module is instantiated.. better management of dependances
=> Composer Autoloading : follows psr-4 standard
-- provide a structure weay to organise the code
-- ideal for large projects with many dependencies
-- standard for autoloading classes based on their namespace prefix to a base directory
1. install composer
2. create composer.json : defines my project's dependencies and autoload settings (look at composer.json)

